From: Ravi <ravi@openloopagentics.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 23:07:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 02/18] Add live widgets, starting with a sparkline

Buttons could only be text, an icon, a clock or a battery readout -- there was
no way to plot a value that changes. At the panel's 2008x60 with ten buttons
each one is a 186x42 cairo surface, which is ample for a real graph.

Add a widget module with a sampled data source and a draw call that receives
the button rectangle, so a widget fills its pill rather than centring a glyph.
This commit ships one kind (sparkline) over two built-in sources (cpu from
/proc/stat deltas, memory from /proc/meminfo), configured with:

  { Widget = "sparkline", Source = "cpu", History = 32, Fill = true,
    Color = "teal" }

Samples are taken on the main loop, which clamps its timeout to 1s while a
widget layer is active; only buttons whose sample changed are marked dirty, so
the existing partial-redraw path still applies. Widgets reuse the Color key
from the palette work for the line colour.

